@namespace Honua.Console.Shell.Components

<section class="console-section">
    <div class="console-page-heading">
        <p class="console-kicker">Publish flow</p>
        <h2>How publishing works</h2>
        <p>One canonical Dataset is exposed through Layers in Services and catalog records (metadata). GeoServices services mirror to the GeoServices service catalog and OGC API Features mirrors to OGC Records as opt-in registrations, default on.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="publish-flow-map">
        <article class="publish-flow-node publish-flow-node-resource">
            <h3>Dataset</h3>
            <p class="publish-flow-kind">Canonical · edited once</p>
            <ul class="publish-flow-steps">
                <li>Source binding</li>
                <li>Fields &amp; semantic roles</li>
                <li>Metadata (ISO 19115, DCAT, STAC)</li>
                <li>Access &amp; presentation defaults</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <div class="publish-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>

        <article class="publish-flow-node">
            <h3>Publish action</h3>
            <p class="publish-flow-kind">7 steps</p>
            <ol class="publish-flow-steps">
                <li>Pick target folder / service</li>
                <li>See compatibility</li>
                <li>Configure the Layer</li>
                <li>Choose field exposure &amp; aliases</li>
                <li>Preview metadata</li>
                <li>Confirm access impact</li>
                <li>Validate &amp; publish (or save draft)</li>
            </ol>
        </article>

        <div class="publish-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>

        <article class="publish-flow-node">
            <h3>Layers</h3>
            <p class="publish-flow-kind">Services · live endpoints</p>
            <div class="publish-slot-row">
                <span class="publish-slot-dot publish-slot-dot-live" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span>FeatureServer endpoint</span>
                <span class="console-status console-state-info">GeoServices service catalog</span>
            </div>
            <div class="publish-slot-row">
                <span class="publish-slot-dot publish-slot-dot-live" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span>OGC API Features collection</span>
                <span class="console-status console-state-info">OGC Records</span>
            </div>
            <p class="publish-flow-kind">Catalog records · metadata</p>
            <div class="publish-record-row">
                <span>GeoServices service catalog / OGC Records</span>
                <span class="console-status console-state-info">auto-mirror</span>
            </div>
            <div class="publish-record-row">
                <span>STAC / DCAT</span>
                <span class="console-status console-state-success">explicit</span>
            </div>
        </article>
    </div>

    <div class="console-panel-grid" style="margin-top:16px;">
        <article class="console-panel">
            <h3>Data access and discovery</h3>
            <p class="console-muted"><strong>Service</strong> — a runtime endpoint that serves data (FeatureServer, OGC API, WMTS). <strong>Catalog record</strong> — metadata about a Dataset with distribution links to its Services.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="console-panel">
            <h3>Catalog registration</h3>
            <p class="console-muted">Publishing to a GeoServices service offers a "Register in GeoServices service catalog" checkbox, default on; the same applies to OGC API Features → OGC Records. Uncheck to keep the service live but hidden from catalog discovery.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="console-panel">
            <h3>Where edits go</h3>
            <p class="console-muted"><strong>Dataset</strong> — meaning, fields, metadata, access defaults. <strong>Layer</strong> — layer id, name, aliases, exposure, cache TTL. <strong>Catalog entry</strong> — follows the service automatically while opted in.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>
